{"name":"Autumn Leaves","hex":"#6e4440","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"autumn leaves","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of autumn leaf"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/autumn_leaves"}],"entries":[{"title":"Autumn leaf color","blocks":[{"text":"Autumn leaf color is a phenomenon that affects the normally green leaves of many deciduous trees and shrubs by which they take on, during a few weeks in the autumn season, various shades of yellow, orange, red, purple, and brown. The phenomenon is commonly called autumn colours or autumn foliage in British English and fall colors, fall foliage, or simply foliage in American English."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Momiji_%E7%B4%85%E8%91%89%E3%81%99%E3%82%8B%E3%83%A4%E3%83%9E%E3%83%A2%E3%83%9F%E3%82%B8_B221212.JPG/330px-Momiji_%E7%B4%85%E8%91%89%E3%81%99%E3%82%8B%E3%83%A4%E3%83%9E%E3%83%A2%E3%83%9F%E3%82%B8_B221212.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Autumn_leaf_color"},{"title":"Autumn Leaves (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Autumn Leaves is a 1956 American psychological drama film directed by Robert Aldrich and starring Joan Crawford in an older woman/younger man tale of mental illness. The film was distributed by Columbia Pictures. The screenplay was written by Jean Rouverol and Hugo Butler, though it was credited to Jack Jevne, since Rouverol and Butler were blacklisted at the time of the film's release."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/fa/Autumn_Leaves_One_Sheet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Autumn_Leaves_(film)"},{"title":"Autumn Leaves (1945 song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Autumn Leaves\" is the English-language lyrical adaptation of the French song \"Les Feuilles mortes\" composed by Joseph Kosma in 1945. The original lyrics were written by Jacques Prévert in French, and in 1950 Johnny Mercer wrote the English lyrics. An instrumental recording by pianist Roger Williams topped the US Billboard charts of 1955."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Autumn_Leaves_(1945_song)"},{"title":"Autumn","blocks":[{"text":"Autumn, also known as fall in North American English, is one of the four temperate seasons on Earth. Outside the tropics, autumn marks the transition from summer to winter, beginning in September or March. Autumn is the season when the duration of daytime becomes noticeably shorter and the temperature cools considerably. Day length decreases and night length increases as the season progresses until the winter solstice in December and June. One of its main features in temperate climates is the striking change in colour of the leaves of deciduous trees as they prepare to shed."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/D%C3%BClmen%2C_Wildpark_--_2014_--_3808_color_balanced.jpg/330px-D%C3%BClmen%2C_Wildpark_--_2014_--_3808_color_balanced.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Autumn"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Kaiserstuhl_-_Herbst_-_Rebblatt_im_Gegenlicht.jpg/500px-Kaiserstuhl_-_Herbst_-_Rebblatt_im_Gegenlicht.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Kaiserstuhl_-_Herbst_-_Rebblatt_im_Gegenlicht.jpg/1280px-Kaiserstuhl_-_Herbst_-_Rebblatt_im_Gegenlicht.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Kaiserstuhl_-_Herbst_-_Rebblatt_im_Gegenlicht.jpg/500px-Kaiserstuhl_-_Herbst_-_Rebblatt_im_Gegenlicht.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKaiserstuhl_-_Herbst_-_Rebblatt_im_Gegenlicht.jpg"